#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_multiplicative.ipynb:270002
#: 5890aa2835d349ad9b209d2ca6173131
msgid "Decomposing contributions in the additive model"
msgstr "Descomposición de las contribuciones en el modelo aditivo"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_multiplicative.ipynb:270004
#: fa2584ab244f4809a23b47a7bfe323d6
msgid ""
"`compute_mean_contributions_over_time()` uses a **unified counterfactual "
"decomposition** for all link types. Each column answers: *\"how much "
"would $\\hat y(t)$ decrease if we removed this component?\"*"
msgstr ""
"`compute_mean_contributions_over_time()` usa una **descomposición "
"contrafactual unificada** para todos los tipos de enlace. Cada columna "
"responde: *\"¿cuánto disminuiría $\\hat y(t)$ si elimináramos este "
"componente?\"*"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_multiplicative.ipynb:270006
#: d87cdd3a3c03457ba2673f5c41308903
msgid "For component $j$ with value $v_j(t)$ in the linear predictor:"
msgstr "Para el componente $j$ con valor $v_j(t)$ en el predictor lineal:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_multiplicative.ipynb:270008
#: 6017ed65e24a441b8cf0ec7c25562b7c
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\text{contribution}_j(t)\n"
"= \\mathbb{E}\\bigl[\\text{inv}(\\mu) \\cdot s\\bigr]\n"
"- \\mathbb{E}\\bigl[\\text{inv}(\\mu - v_j) \\cdot s\\bigr]\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\text{contribution}_j(t)\n"
"= \\mathbb{E}\\bigl[\\text{inv}(\\mu) \\cdot s\\bigr]\n"
"- \\mathbb{E}\\bigl[\\text{inv}(\\mu - v_j) \\cdot s\\bigr]\n"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_multiplicative.ipynb:270014
#: 0d8db2cb2de4442d9c18445e111f5697
#, python-brace-format
msgid "where $\\text{inv}$ is the inverse link and $s$ = `target_scale`."
msgstr "donde $\\text{inv}$ es el enlace inverso y $s$ = `target_scale`."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_multiplicative.ipynb:270016
#: 619c1d72e1974fa390f9e30152c00d06
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"With an identity link $\\text{inv}$ is the identity function, so this "
"simplifies to:"
msgstr ""
"Con un enlace identidad, $\\text{inv}$ es la función identidad, por lo que "
"esto se simplifica a:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_multiplicative.ipynb:270018
#: 31ead01469314acfb960b391caefcf8f
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\text{contribution}_j(t) = \\mathbb{E}[v_j(t)] \\cdot s\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\text{contribution}_j(t) = \\mathbb{E}[v_j(t)] \\cdot s\n"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_multiplicative.ipynb:270022
#: 59effa60ef91437f87a8672e7fb31427
msgid ""
"The resulting columns **sum exactly to $\\hat y(t)$** at every date. Each"
" line in the decomposition plot below can be read as *\"this many units "
"of $y$ came from this component on this date.\"*"
msgstr ""
"Las columnas resultantes **suman exactamente $\\hat y(t)$** en cada fecha. "
"Cada línea del gráfico de descomposición siguiente puede leerse como "
"*\"estas unidades de $y$ provinieron de este componente en esta fecha.\"*"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_multiplicative.ipynb:300002
#: 1c246051f215487496af5cbce19ecbfb
msgid ""
"The line plot shows each component's time-varying contribution in "
"original-scale units."
msgstr ""
"El gráfico de líneas muestra la contribución variable en el tiempo de cada "
"componente en unidades de la escala original."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_multiplicative.ipynb:310002
#: c19877fd483d4bc0a51b51ac11b07bc5
msgid ""
"In many cases, we are not just interested in the posterior mean "
"decomposition, but the entire distribution of contributions. We can also "
"extract this from the model:"
msgstr ""
"En muchos casos, no nos interesa solo la descomposición de la media "
"posterior, sino toda la distribución de las contribuciones. También podemos "
"extraerla del modelo:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_multiplicative.ipynb:340002
#: 5561518cb74344e688f3acda895e7506
msgid ""
"To summarize the relative importance of the two media channels we can "
"look at their posterior share distributions below."
msgstr ""
"Para resumir la importancia relativa de los dos canales de medios, podemos "
"observar sus distribuciones posteriores de proporción a continuación."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_multiplicative.ipynb:360002
#: 6b8e7716831a461ba37fe7ca9ebb5a92
msgid ""
"Channel `x1` captures the majority of the estimated media effect, "
"consistent with its higher spend volume. The posterior distributions are "
"well separated, giving confidence that the model can distinguish the two "
